WEBVTT

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.360
"Kodomo no Odocha"

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.700
That rumor that I love you

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.330
is true, yes it is.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.830
You can't ignore it either.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.420
Whether you're awake or asleep,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.050
please don't be embarrassed.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.680
Is it a sin if I sneak into your heart

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.310
by ridding you...

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.480
...of your other love?

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.060
At sunset,

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.570
when the children go home,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.490
Today's incident is burning love!

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.410
You can tell it accurately.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.490
7 O'Clock News!

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.290
Please, our relationship...

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:09.960
Please don't blame it on the true kiss

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.800
In a city without light,

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.680
let's burn the fire of love.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.100
Don't be so easy going

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.350
The existence is a mistake

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.850
You're asking for something not there.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.860
I'm Kurata Sana, a 6th grader
and TV personality.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.870
My beloved Mama is a famous
Aoki-award winning novelist.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:42.200
My manager, chauffeur,
and former boyfriend, Sagami Rei-kun.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.870
The mysterious white bat straight man.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.200
I'm Babbit.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.210
Hayama Akito, my natural enemy
and good friend.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:50.880
Father Hayama.
Father, the background is too dark.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.050
Sana-chan, come visit us again soon.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.930
"Love-Love, Father Hayama's Song"

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.350
Ah, autumn!

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.680
Autumn...

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.680
I love autumn! After all...

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:09.350
Delicious roasted sweet potatoes!

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:11.690
...it's the season that the roasted
sweet-potato truck comes around!

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:13.020
Sana-chan...

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:14.900
"Come to think of it,
Hayama's name is..."

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:17.740
Aki!! Hayama, your name
is Aki-to! ("Autumn")

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.070
If you're named after autumn,
then by any chance...

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.410
Hayama! You were born during autumn,
weren't you?

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.080
Yeah.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.080
How sharply deduced of me!

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.080
Shut up.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.750
So, when is it?

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:30.080
Your birthday. I've been
meaning to ask for a while now.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.340
October 12th.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.670
Oh, no! That's tomorrow!
Let's have a party! A b-b-big blowout!

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:36.340
Sana-chan...!

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:38.680
It's okay,
Tsuyoshi-kun, you're invited!

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.010
It's not that...

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:43.010
I go visit the cemetery
on my birthday every year.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.020
Oh, crap!

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:50.690
I forgot. His birthday also equals
the anniversary of his mother's death.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.860
H- have you, by any chance--
and I'm not saying you wouldn't have--

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:56.690
ever had a birthday party, Hayama?

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:57.360
Nope.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.030
Never? None at all? Not even once?

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.370
No. Every year, I visit the cemetery.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:05.370
H- how depressing.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.370
My birthday means the scent of incense.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:11.370
It's no wonder you're
so warped and everything.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.710
Let's have a party, Hayama!

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.040
I said I'm going to visit the cemetery.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.500
I don't mean that!
There's something popular

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.720
going around with the girls
these days. "Middle birthdays."

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.050
Middle birthdays?

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.380
What are those, Sana-chan?

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:24.850
You see, you have a party and
exchange presents on the day

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.060
right in the middle
of your two birthdays.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.060
Let's see, mine is on March 7th, so...

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:34.650
1, 2, 3, 4... um... uh...

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.900
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6... carry the 2...

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.320
no, that doesn't have
anything to do with it...

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.990
1, 2, 3, 4, 5... this isn't
crane-and-turtle math, right? S- six...?

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.200
"One moment please"

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.200
Yeah, she's kind of weak at math,
so this will take a little time.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.700
Oh?

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.000
It's Christmas Eve!

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.040
Party on Christmas Eve! A birthday party
and gift exchange!

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.380
It's settled! It's settled!

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.040
Don't go deciding that for all of us.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:03.680
♪ Ba-bing, thwack, Ave Maria! ♪

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:18.070
"Abominable Snowman Hayama"

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.350
♪ Middle party on Christmas Eve! ♪

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:11.020
♪ Jingle joyous Christmas Eve, ♪

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:14.400
♪ Jingle, Christ-sama's birthday! ♪

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.070
I think Christ-sama's birthday
is on the 25th.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.360
Never mind that...

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.030
Never mind!?

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.700
Would you two go with me?

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.700
Go with you?

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:27.700
To the cemetery.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.080
What for?

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.660
I think my mom would like to see
something unusual once in a while.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.000
Hey, what am I, some strange animal!?
An X-File!?

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.250
Can't you just split your butt

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.670
and say you want to introduce
your friends to her, you...!?

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:38.670
Now, now, Sana-chan,

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.000
Rawr! Rowr!

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.010
"A cemetery visit
with the Hayama Family"

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:47.010
Oh, this is an
unusual sight for Kodocha.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:50.100
Oh, the rustic train station,
the sweet air...

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.350
Thank goodness the weather is nice.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:56.650
Yeah.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.690
This father and son still
don't talk to each other much.

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:06.030
Sana-chan and Tsuyoshi-kun,
thanks for coming with us.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.030
Not at all.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:09.780
We came because Hayama
invited us to come,

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.040
but are you sure we're not in the way?

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.370
I'm all excitable, and a
little bit of a chatterbox, and all...

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.040
A little bit?

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.040
Are you saying I'm not!?

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.380
Now, now, Sana-chan.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.710
I'm always having to do this.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:23.300
Koharu-- my wife, liked things lively,

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.380
so I'm sure she'll be thrilled
to have Sana-chan here.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:28.720
Oh? That's the kind
of person she was, huh?

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.970
Y- yes... yes she was. Akito,

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:37.310
your mother...

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.520
your mother, see...

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.360
your mother...

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:46.990
that is to say...

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.990
...s- she liked things lively.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:54.330
Y- you just barely told us that,
Father Hayama...!

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.580
So what is it you're trying
to say, Father Hayama?

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.670
Well, I'm going to go give
my respects to the head priest,

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.340
so you all go on ahead.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.750
--Okay.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:15.430
Wow, a very, very, beautiful lady!

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:22.020
Hayama, who was that?

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:23.360
I don't know.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.360
But she nodded when
she saw you, Akito-kun.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:27.030
I still don't know her.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:30.030
For some reason, it seems like
I've seen her somewhere before,

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.320
but then again, maybe not...

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.660
Which is it?

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.660
Doesn't matter which one.
Let's get going.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.000
But it's bothering me!

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.660
Now, now, Sana-chan...
Ah, I'm saying it again!

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.370
"Hayama says 'Eh!?'"

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.500
Eh?

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.010
Say, didn't those flowers
come from Beautiful earlier?

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:47.340
They must be.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.680
Maybe she's one of Mom's friends.
Dad might know her.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:53.680
It's not "Battobi," it's "Babbit"!

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.350
A mysterious Beautiful?

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:57.680
That's right! She didn't remind me of
those moai statues on Easter Island,

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.310
she reminded me a little more of
the Statue of Liberty in New York--

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.690
that type of woman.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:02.360
Moai?

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:04.020
He can't tell anything from that.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.360
She looked a little younger
than you, Dad.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:10.700
She was pale, her hair was long,
and she seemed pretty elegant.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.030
That's right, I could do that, huh?

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:16.370
Yeah.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:21.040
Huh? Eh? Hey, Father Hayama, hello...?

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.380
Sana-chan, thanks for
coming along today.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:26.050
You said that a long while ago.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:28.130
Your tempo is a bit slow today,
isn't it?

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:31.300
Mother Hayama, it's nice to meet you.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:36.310
My name is Kurata Sana.
Your little boy is a bit of a scamp,

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:40.980
but he's still a pretty good guy,
so don't you worry.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:44.110
"Cemetery visit complete"

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:44.150
Okay, the serene visit to the
cemetery is over, and that evening...

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:46.980
...and as a result,

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:49.990
I wound up missing out
on hearing about Beautiful.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.990
What!?

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:54.990
That attitude of Father Hayama's
sure is suspicious!

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:02.710
I've got it! I'll bet Beautiful is
really Father Hayama's secret lover!

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.340
Father Hayama is in love-love!

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:08.000
Father Hayama's in love-love!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.010
Sana-chan, Sana-chan,
you mustn't believe that!

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.010
Sensei is currently
writing a romance novel,

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.340
so she has been bringing love-love
into everything she sees!

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.350
Life is a dazzling trip
down the lost path of love...

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:18.010
See?

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:21.310
You're right. Ah, you startled me!

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.350
Imagine, Father Hayama
having a girlfriend!

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:26.770
Still, it wouldn't be surprising
if there was such a woman,

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.690
and he was talking about remarrying.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:30.110
She's right.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:34.950
As I recall, it has been over ten years
since Hayama-kun's mother passed away.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.320
Then, right now,
Father Hayama really is...

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.330
Love-love Father Hayama!?

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:44.290
♪ Aah, living in this world, ♪

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:49.340
♪ rose in hand, floating
along on the water... ♪

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.630
"Love-love Father Hayama!?"

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.670
How was my pop acting?

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:55.970
Mm-hmm. Did he do anything
strange afterward?

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:56.970
Not really.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:09:00.310
But he was definitely acting
strange at the cemetery, huh?

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.020
Yeah, yeah, like he had an alligator
stuck in his back teeth,

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.690
and was about to say something,
but then stopped.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.650
You can't get an alligator
stuck in your back teeth.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:08.360
Ah, it got stuck!

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.020
Babbit, you're a disgrace
to the whole family!

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:12.690
You know, perchance, conceivably,
it's possible that...

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.280
Hayama let's out a slight 'eh!'

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:16.990
Girlfriend?

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.660
That pretty lady was
your father's girlfriend!?

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:22.040
That's the right
reaction to have, Hayama!

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.330
Is that right?

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.710
That couldn't be.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:27.000
Yeah, you're right. I don't
think it's that, either.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.670
But the world can turn the tables
on you. Even Rei-kun had a girlfriend.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.630
Yeah, you're right.
That sometimes happens, too, huh?

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:33.630
Doesn't it though?

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:36.300
Hey there, stick with your own ideas!

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.300
Hayama, it's the truth, I tell you.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.640
No, it's not.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:41.310
--It absolutely is.
--...that was so funny when that happened!

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.310
--It's absolutely not.
--...that was so funny when that happened!

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.140
It sure was.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:49.060
Hey, watch out!

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.980
D- did you see that?
You saw that, right?

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.990
I knew it! I knew it! I knew it!
Those two are lovers!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:58.320
T- then again, maybe they're
friends from work, or something.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:09:59.660
Naive!

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:02.200
Father Hayama's attitude when we
visited the cemetery was suspicious--

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:05.330
too suspicious--
an eruption of suspicion!

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.330
He didn't even make this face!

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:09.000
They went into that shop!

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:12.340
How can we not
investigate this, Washington-kun?

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.670
Watson-kun!

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:16.010
My investigative blood is boiling!

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.340
Hayama-kun, where are you going?

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.680
I'm going home.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.340
What about our investigative mission!?

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:21.680
Do it yourself.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.350
I will do it myself, and I'll be fine!

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.680
Let's go, Vaseline-kun!

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:28.020
It's Watson-kun! Why don't
you read the novel!?

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:31.270
Forgive me for calling on
you like this, Shiori-san.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:35.610
Not at all. Natsumi-chan and
Akito-kun sure have grown up, huh?

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:39.610
The reason for my heartfelt
request has to do with Akito.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:40.610
There they are!

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:41.950
What do we do?

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.910
Come on, let's go!

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.950
Hold on there, you guys!

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:48.960
This is no place for
children to be playing!

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.290
This is a place to drink tea!

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.290
Then I'll have a cappuccino.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.630
Um, a strawberry parfait.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:56.300
D- don't we look
awfully strange right now?

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.630
Whenever a person earnestly
dives into doing something,

00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.970
they are more beautiful than anything.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.930
I don't know...

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.310
Ha, ha, ha, that is funny.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.310
Positively. That producer kills me.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:09.980
Huh!?

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:11.650
It's you, awl right, Sana-chan!

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:12.980
Sana-chan?

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:14.650
This is bad!

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.320
Sana-chan!

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:17.650
Is something the matter?

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.650
Oh, no, I thought I heard
the name of a girl that I know.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:24.660
Ah, this dust.
I'm wearing contacts, and all...

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:26.660
See here, Sana-chan, what did
you do that for awl of a sudden!?

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:29.000
That was terrible, Zenjiro-san!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.000
Do you realize what you've just done?

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.000
Huh?

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.340
What did I do?

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:36.340
How awful...

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:38.670
How awful!

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:41.010
A-awful...?

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:44.090
Awful? Really? I'm awful, huh?

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:46.350
Now that I think about it,
I had no idea I was so...

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.020
What about Father!?

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:53.020
It's not like that, Sana-chan!
She's having trouble with her contacts--

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:55.360
Bingo!!

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:59.860
Father Hayama! You're already
thinking of marriage!?

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.740
Peeping, huh?

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:13.960
That was totally love-love!

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.960
I saw it too. It's true.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:16.960
Hayama, what are you going to do?

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.300
I'm not doing anything.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.630
Oh, you're planning to play it cool
through till the end, huh?

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.970
Watch, we're going to
reenact the love-love scene!

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.640
Look, look, they were lovers,
just like this!

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:27.970
Are you sure about that?

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.310
I'm home.

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:30.640
Oh, Sister Hayama.

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:31.980
--Listen, something terrible is happening!
--I saw it! At that coffee shop

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.270
--I don't know what your father is thinking,
--that has terrible strawberry parfait!

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:34.520
--but suddenly he's in love-love.
--Your father, who's not so young anymore,

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.770
--Isn't that a shock?
--was embarrassing himself
with this very pretty woman!

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.610
Huh!? Dad has a girlfriend!?

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:41.940
Unfortunately, in my estimation,
there can be no mistake about it.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:44.950
She is the same Beautiful
from the visit to the cemetery.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:45.950
I remember now.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:47.620
--Huh? What?

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:48.620
"The identity of Beautiful...!"

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.620
Let's see... Look, look, here she is!

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:51.290
Here.

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.290
She's in this picture with Mom.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.630
Oh, it's Beautiful! Is that one of
Mother Hayama's old photo albums?

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:58.630
Ah, she's in this one, too.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:02.300
She was one of Mom's friends.
That explains why I remember seeing her.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.630
Oh, so she's just
one of her friends, then.

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:06.640
Naive!

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:08.970
This is more dangerous
than anything, sir.

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:12.810
He bumps into his late wife's friend,
and suddenly remarries!

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.310
It happens quite frequently in dramas.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.640
Oh, no.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.310
I don't like this.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:21.070
I always thought that
the children in those dramas

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:23.320
who opposed their parent getting
remarried were being narrow-minded,

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:26.320
but when I'm put in the same position,
I don't like it.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:29.330
I don't know exactly why,
but I just don't like it!

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:30.990
Hayama, what about you?

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:32.910
I don't know.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:36.000
I don't have any memory
of my mom, after all.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.250
I don't know from a new mom,
or my real mom.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.500
S- still, even if you don't
have any memories of her,

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.920
you've heard your father
reminisce about her, right?

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:43.920
No.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:44.920
Really?

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:49.050
Back when I was little,
he used to talk a lot about Mom,

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:50.260
but he hardly ever does so now.

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:51.260
Why not?

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:55.930
He probably doesn't want to be reminded.
She died giving birth to me, and all.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.270
Ah, this is not good!

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:02.610
--W- what's going on here, Father Hayama!?
--She caught me!

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:05.280
You finally got over being
a chicken-and-egg dum-dum,

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:07.150
and now you won't even tell one story
to your son about his mother!

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:08.950
You only think about your own love-love!

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:11.950
Sana-chan, we still
aren't certain about that.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.950
She's right. If this were one of
those dramas, then in this situation,

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.960
he would first say "there's somebody
that I'd like you to meet," or something.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:18.960
I'm home.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.630
There you are, Father Hayama!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.630
Sana-chan, Tsuyoshi-kun,
you're over, huh?

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:23.960
Oh, yes.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:25.960
By the way, Natsumi and Akito,

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:29.300
as it happens, there's somebody
that I'd like you to meet.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:33.260
Her name is Daiichi Shiori-san,
and she was your mom's best friend.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:38.230
She is a very kind, nice person,
so I'm sure you two will like her.

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:42.270
I know this is sudden,
but she'll be coming over tonight.

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:44.900
E- excuse us for just a minute!

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:48.900
No! No! Sana-chan, what do we do!?

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.780
This is another sudden
troubling development!

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:52.280
What should we-- should we--
should we-- Sri Lanka!?

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:54.950
What are you going to do, Akito-kun?
This is bad!

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:56.250
Not really.

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:59.290
This is unfair, Dad! You've been
keeping it secret up to now,

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.920
and now you're suddenly
having her come over today!

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:04.550
Unfair? Oh, Mama mentioned
that word once.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:11.930
Remember, Sana, sometimes in life,
it is wise for people to fight unfairly.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:15.970
If you think you're in the right,
you can use all sorts of dirty tricks.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:18.930
When is this anime going to become
suitable for good little children?

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.270
If they're not going to play fair,

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:22.310
then we can launch our own
dirty campaign, right?

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:23.560
Dirty campaign?

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:27.940
We'll call it "Operation 'l'm Shocked,
and I've Completely Had It With You!'"

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:29.650
Okay, Baby's Rock!

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.320
W- what sort of plan is it?

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:35.910
We're going to make
Shiori-san hate Father Hayama.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.910
Enough that she won't want to
see him for the rest of his life.

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:40.580
Oh, there's no way
anyone can stop her now.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:42.250
Incoming!

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.920
There it is!

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.920
Rei-kun! Rei-kun! There's something
I want you to bring me

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.920
"Burutcha secret code transmission"

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:46.920
without letting Mama know!

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.420
"Kurata Sana's Burutcha Code
At-a-Glance"

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.420
Understood! Don't move
from that spot, Sana-chan!

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:51.930
Yes?

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:55.260
Huh? An emergency neighborhood
association meeting?

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:58.270
At the Asagane Ward Center?
That far away?

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:01.940
Yes, beginning at 7 o'clock.
We really need you to be there.

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:03.940
All right then, goodbye now.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:04.940
"V"!

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:07.610
Sana-chan, are you sure we
should be telling lies like that?

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:10.190
Not to worry! Just call it
my "Mission, Mark II."

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.610
Are you sure you'll
be fine by yourselves?

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:15.950
We're fine, we're fine.
Shiori-san is a nice person, right?

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.290
Dad, you just relax and go
to the association meeting.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:20.620
You're sure? Okay then...

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:21.960
Be back soon!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.290
All right, he's gone!

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:25.630
All righty, begin the operation!

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:26.750
"She's here..."

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.300
Good evening.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:31.130
Good evening!

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:34.550
So, your father had to go out, did he?

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:37.970
Yes, something suddenly came up.
Be my guest.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:41.890
Such an odd interior...

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.890
It's decorated to
Father Hayama's tastes!

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.560
'lo there!

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:46.900
Here, here, please, have a seat.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:50.570
Yes, Father Hayama buys the most unique
and trivial things by mail order.

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:53.900
What's more, he wears this
on his head around the house!

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:56.240
And that's not all, ma'am.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.660
Once he took a picture of
his department head making out,

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.240
and ran riot around his company!

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:02.910
On top of that, no sooner
does he goes bungee jumping...

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:06.920
...than he becomes a dancer who wears
a mask, because he can't show his face,

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.590
and after all else, he suddenly snaps...

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:10.250
I'm mad!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:13.260
...he turns his desk upside-down
and goes wild inside the classroom!

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:16.260
I'm surprised at how well Sana-chan
can make up such a silly story.

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.260
This is what you guys
normally do, you know!

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:21.600
As you can see, Father Hayama is
a very eccentric man, Shiori-san.

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:24.600
Ah, this car and person's weight dummy
are also Father's. Isn't that weird?

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:28.360
You should think twice about
getting too close to Father Hayama!

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:32.320
Sakurai-san, aren't you going

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.900
to the neighborhood association's
emergency meeting?

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.780
What do you mean?

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:40.580
Hayama-san is a stranger man than
you'd think from looking at him, huh?

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:44.250
You understand, don't you? I'm so glad.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:48.250
Now then, I've heard all
these stories about Hayama-san,

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:51.250
so now, why don't I tell
some stories of my own?

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:53.260
Wow, you're persistent.

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:56.260
Okay then, here comes the
final weapon against Father Hayama!

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:56.930
Final weapon?

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.760
Once you see this
last peculiarity about him,

00:17:58.760 --> 00:17:59.930
you'll reconsider and be
absolutely fed up with him!

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:01.930
Okay, Father Hayama,
the Nori-nori machine!

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:04.270
He's a shocking father,
our Father Hayama!

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:06.270
He's a shocking father,
our Father Hayama.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.440
--♪ He's a shocking father, ♪
--♪ He's a shocking father, ♪

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:08.270
--♪ our Father Hayama! ♪
--♪ our Father Hayama! ♪

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.400
--♪ Anywhere he goes, ♪
--♪ Anywhere he goes, ♪

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:12.270
--♪ father is a strange old man! ♪
--♪ father is a strange old man! ♪

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.440
--♪ He stops in mid-sentence, ♪
--♪ He stops in mid-sentence, ♪

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:14.610
--♪ and talks to the TV! ♪
--♪ and talks to the TV! ♪

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:18.610
♪ But I'm still a pretty swell pop. ♪

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:19.990
♪ I'm not a good speaker, ♪

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.950
♪ since I'm just a little shy. ♪

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.620
♪ But I'm still a dandy Father Hayama. ♪

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:26.960
♪ My playful little mustache
is my most charming point. ♪

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:30.290
♪ Oh my, why is Daddy singing... ♪

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:34.550
♪ ...by himself? ♪

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.550
Goodness, Father Hayama,
you're home early...

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:38.220
We're still over...

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.220
Dad!

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:41.550
Natsumi, what is all this?

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:45.560
It's just... it's just, Dad,
it's too soon for marriage!

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.230
Marriage?

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.890
Well, of course it is.

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:51.560
You're still in your third year
of middle school. Marriage would be...

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:54.900
Not me! I mean your marriage, Dad!

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:59.910
I was 24 when I married your mother.
By no means do I think that was too soon.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.240
No, Father Hayama,
your marriage to Shiori-san!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:06.580
Ah, Sana-chan, you're over, are you?

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.500
That is why you invited
Shiori-san over here today, right?

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.500
Then, judging from your reaction,

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:13.920
Father Hayama, don't tell me,
could it be, possibly...?

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:16.920
You guys have it all wrong.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:21.840
Akito-kun, your father said he
wanted me to personally tell you

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.930
some stories about your mother.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:27.890
Shiori-san, as you know,
up until just recently,

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:30.600
I had been a failure as a father.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:33.860
I put Akito through a lot of misery.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:36.900
Akito doesn't have
any memories of his mom.

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:41.450
As his father, I think I should
tell him all about his mom,

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.570
but I'm just not that good at speaking.

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:46.910
That's why, if I could, I'd like
to have you tell him, Shiori-san.

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:49.080
I'm sorry, Akito.

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:52.120
I did all this without knowing that!?

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.880
I'm so embarrassed!
I'm beyond embarrassed!

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.880
--How could I have done such a thing!?
--I'm embarrassed myself.

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:57.920
--How embarrassing!
--And here I'm in the
3rd grade of middle school...

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:00.220
Well, I guess I'm embarrassed, too.

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:01.630
"Let's reflect on this"

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:01.630
You really are idiots.

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:04.260
This week's Sana-chan.

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:06.260
I already said
I was embarrassed, you know.

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:12.140
Your mother and I were good friends
ever since high school.

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:16.150
Your mother was a cheerful person,
whose expressions were always changing.

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:18.820
But the things she said were
sometimes a little strange.

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.820
Hey, Shiori, isn't winter great?

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:21.820
You think so?

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:22.820
After all,

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:26.160
we get to eat lots of
mochi rice cakes at New Year's!

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:28.160
And then, when spring came around...

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.830
Hey, isn't spring great?

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:30.830
Uh-huh.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:34.170
After all, we get to eat sakuramochi
and kashiwamochi rice cakes!

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.170
And then, when summer came around...

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:38.170
Ah, isn't summer great?

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.170
Oh, yeah?

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:42.630
After all, we get to eat
snow-cones and watermelon!

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:47.850
And then, when autumn came,
she said "Isn't autumn great?"

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:50.180
When I asked her if it was because
she could eat tsukimidango dumplings

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:51.180
and roast sweet-potatoes,

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:55.850
she was honestly surprised. "Shiori, how
did you know? How? How?" she asked me.

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:58.520
Was she just a glutton?

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:01.190
Not at all.

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:05.860
Say, Shiori, I always get excited
when a new season comes along.

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:08.200
Even if I'm depressed,
or something is bothering me,

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:10.910
whenever a new season comes, I always
feel like "let's give it a go!"

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:13.210
or "just hang in there!"

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:18.210
That's why I love them. Fall, spring,
summer, autumn-- I love them all!

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:22.880
Which is why, Natsumi-chan and Akito-kun,
your mom gave you the names that she did.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:25.220
The names of the seasons
in which you were born.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:28.890
I remember the summer you
were in her tummy, Akito-kun.

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:31.560
This baby is going to be born in October,
so I'm going to name him Akito,

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:33.560
which will be written
"Autumn person"-- "Aki-to."

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:35.560
What will you do if it's a girl?

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:39.980
He's a boy. I can tell.
For some reason, I can tell.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:42.570
The same was true for Natsumi.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:45.240
My adorable little...

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:46.240
...Natsumi...

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:47.240
...Akito...

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:48.570
After that, you mother--

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:49.570
That's enough.

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:50.580
Hey, Akito...

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:51.580
Really?

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:53.910
Thanks. As for the rest of it...

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:55.910
Hey, Hayama! Don't go out
into the yard without shoes on!

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:57.580
There are sandals out there.

00:21:57.580 --> 00:21:58.580
Hayama-san...

00:21:58.580 --> 00:21:59.250
Yes?

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:03.210
Akito-kun said he wants to hear
the rest out of his father's mouth,

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:04.590
in his father's words.

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:05.920
I see...

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:08.180
Looks like everything
turned out all right, huh?

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:09.550
It was worth all the
effort we put into it.

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:12.430
Remember what it was that you did!

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:17.190
Hayama, that was your
birthday present, huh?

00:22:17.190 --> 00:22:20.560
The name "Akito,"
from a very fine mother.

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:21.520
Y- yeah...

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:22.190
Getting self-conscious?

00:22:22.230 --> 00:22:23.230
Shut up.

00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:24.860
All righty, shall we sing?

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:25.900
What for?

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:27.860
He's a shocking father,
our Father Hayama!

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:29.570
--Anywhere he goes,
father is a strange old man!
--Cut it out.

00:22:29.570 --> 00:22:31.530
--He's a very eccentric dad!
--Stop it.

00:22:31.530 --> 00:22:33.540
--But he's still a fine dad!
--Let go.

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:35.910
Yeah, a very fine dad!

00:22:35.910 --> 00:22:37.870
A fine dad, just like his son!

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:40.580
Let's go, let's go, let's go, let's go!

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:42.250
"Back against the wall."

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:47.720
That's what you say about times like these.

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:52.470
In dire straits,

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:56.060
I've been waiting for an answer.

00:22:56.560 --> 00:22:59.940
My confessions are worked out
long in advance,

00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:05.030
to always go along with the scenario.

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:11.070
My heart may be settled, but my mind is in a...

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:13.280
...panic!!

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:19.120
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:21.830
he's there.

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:25.090
And our usual classroom...

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:27.670
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:30.180
...for two.

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:33.640
Although I've said nothing but wisecracks...

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:38.390
...up to now, just for today,

00:23:39.310 --> 00:23:41.980
I'm going to be honest and sincere,

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:46.690
so BOY, take a look my way!

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:52.280
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:54.950
he's there,

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:58.120
And our usual classroom...

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:00.710
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:03.210
...for two.

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:09.670
Hoy! In Sana-chan's next adventures...

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:13.340
Mama is seriously nervous!
My mother's mother is Mama's Mama.

00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:15.550
My grandma is even
more amazing than Mama.

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:17.010
She has come to arrange
a marriage for Mama!

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:21.020
She brought a whole host of the kind
of candidates that Mama doesn't like!

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:25.690
Next time on Kodomo no Omocha,
Episode 29, the Disruptive Grandma
from the Hot Spring Resort saga,

00:24:25.690 --> 00:24:31.030
She's Here! Mother's Mother

00:24:31.030 --> 00:24:35.570
Sana-chan, you're always
such a sorry fool.
